docs/implementation-plan.md-2-
docs/implementation-plan.md:3:This is the working plan for building Curator, an agent environment manager (AEM) in Go. Iterations consult this document and the task board; the plan is updated as decisions land. Protocol sections are cited as `Spec §N.M` against the 1.0.0-rc.2 [Curator Specification](https://github.com/relux-works/curator-spec).
docs/implementation-plan.md-4-
docs/implementation-plan.md-5-## 1. Goal and definition of done
docs/implementation-plan.md-6-
docs/implementation-plan.md:7:Curator v0.1 is a conforming independent implementation of the protocol: it works with the same skill packages, the same project manifests, the same installed layouts, and the same audit registries as the reference implementation, per the eight conformance requirements of Spec §17.1. Done means:
docs/implementation-plan.md-8-
docs/implementation-plan.md-9-1. All conformance-relevant behavior is implemented and covered by tests, including the golden interoperability suite (Section 6 below).
docs/implementation-plan.md-10-2. `curator` installs a real project from `Skillfile.json` end to end on macOS, Linux, and Windows.
--
docs/implementation-plan.md-20-| Language | Go 1.23+ | Static binaries, first-class Windows, stdlib `crypto/ed25519` |
docs/implementation-plan.md-21-| Module | `github.com/relux-works/curator` | Public repository |
docs/implementation-plan.md-22-| CLI framework | stdlib `flag` with a small subcommand dispatcher | The CLI surface is informative in the spec; avoid framework lock-in. Revisit only if UX demands it |
docs/implementation-plan.md:23:| Git operations | shell out to system `git` with `GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL=file:git:http:https:ssh`, URLs passed after `--` | Matches Spec §8.2 transport restrictions exactly; no libgit2/go-git divergence risk |
docs/implementation-plan.md-24-| JSON | stdlib `encoding/json` with strict unknown-field rejection where the spec requires it | Spec §5.1, §6.1 |
docs/implementation-plan.md-25-| TOML (codex configs) | `github.com/BurntSushi/toml` | Read-only MCP surface parsing (Spec §11.1) |
docs/implementation-plan.md-26-| JSONC (opencode) | minimal in-repo comment stripper, then stdlib JSON | One surface, trivial grammar; no dependency |
--
docs/implementation-plan.md-29-| TUI (later phase) | `bubbletea` + `lipgloss`; tests with `tuitestkit` from skill-go-testing-tools | Closed-loop TUI testing |
docs/implementation-plan.md-30-| Testing | stdlib `testing`, table-driven; authoritative vectors from `curator-spec/conformance/v1` | Deterministic and shared by independent implementations |
docs/implementation-plan.md-31-| Lint/CI | `gofmt`, `go vet`, `golangci-lint`, GitHub Actions matrix (ubuntu, macos, windows) | Windows is first class |
docs/implementation-plan.md:32:| Layout | `cmd/curator/` (main), `internal/<domain>/` packages mirroring protocol domains | Spec-traceable package boundaries |
docs/implementation-plan.md-33-| Machine home | `~/.curator/` (env `CURATOR_CONFIG`, `CURATOR_SYSTEM_CONFIG`; system config `/etc/curator/config.json`, `%ProgramData%\curator`) | The machine home is tool-specific state (config, caches, runtime store), not a wire format; two managers on one machine must not share it. Shared wire formats stay exactly as specified: `Skillfile.json`, canonical `agent-skill.json`, legacy `csk-skill.json`, markers, adapter ledgers |
docs/implementation-plan.md-34-
docs/implementation-plan.md-35-Package sketch: `internal/skillspec`, `internal/manifest`, `internal/devsub`, `internal/config`, `internal/identity`, `internal/gitops`, `internal/snapshot`, `internal/hashing`, `internal/closure`, `internal/whitelist`, `internal/locale`, `internal/marker`, `internal/runtimestore`, `internal/shims`, `internal/adapters`, `internal/mcp`, `internal/scopes` (global, hybrid, consumers, gc), `internal/registry`, `internal/audit`, `internal/shell`, `internal/cli`.
