docs/implementation-plan.md-38-
docs/implementation-plan.md-39-- Tasks live on the in-repo board `.task-board/` (epics, stories, tasks as directories with `README.md` and `progress.md`; artifacts in `.task-board/.resources/<ID>/`). Every change starts from a task; progress and status are updated as work proceeds.
docs/implementation-plan.md-40-- Commits are discrete and meaningful: one logical step per commit, imperative subject, body explaining what and why. Signed (SSH key, verified on GitHub) as Ivan Oparin <oparin@me.com>.
docs/implementation-plan.md:41:- The name of the alternative protocol implementation appears exactly once: the README open-protocol section. A CI check greps case-insensitively (zero matches outside README.md, exactly one inside). The protocol is cited as `Spec §N.M` against [curator-spec](https://github.com/relux-works/curator-spec); protocol file names (`Skillfile.json`, `agent-skill.json`, legacy `csk-skill.json`, `.csk-install.json`, `.csk-managed.json`) are part of the wire format and are used as-is.
docs/implementation-plan.md-42-- Spec first: when implementation and spec disagree, stop and resolve the spec question before coding around it.
docs/implementation-plan.md-43-- Every error message that the spec words normatively (allowlist refusal, MCP hint, conflicts with chains) keeps the same information content, not necessarily the same string.
docs/implementation-plan.md-44-- Style for prose (docs, board cards): plain technical English, no em dashes, no guillemets.
--
