docs/implementation-plan.md-129-- Unit: table-driven per MUST clause, typed error assertions.
docs/implementation-plan.md-130-- Integration: temp-dir projects with real git repositories built in test setup; full install cycles; idempotence (second install is `up-to-date`); tamper detection.
docs/implementation-plan.md:131:- Interop: the external versioned protocol suite (Phase 10) as the conformance gate.
docs/implementation-plan.md-132-- TUI: tuitestkit closed-loop (Phase 11).
docs/implementation-plan.md-133-- Windows: everything runs in the CI matrix; path handling tested with `win_path`, `.cmd` shims, `%ProgramData%` system config.
docs/implementation-plan.md-134-
docs/implementation-plan.md-135-## 7. Risks and watchpoints
docs/implementation-plan.md-136-
docs/implementation-plan.md:137:- Byte-compatibility of the content hash and marker JSON is the highest-risk surface; build Phase 2 hashing against the shared protocol vectors first.
docs/implementation-plan.md-138-- JSON field ordering in markers: the spec fixes content, not key order; markers are compared as parsed objects, hashes as bytes.
docs/implementation-plan.md-139-- Windows symlink permissions: adapter `auto` mode must degrade to copy without failing (Spec §10.1).
docs/implementation-plan.md-140-- Git version drift across CI runners: pin behaviors by testing outcomes, not stdout strings.
--
README.md-2-
README.md-3-Curator is an agent environment manager (AEM): a single tool that manages what an AI coding agent gets in a project. Skills and their transitive dependencies, executable commands, MCP server requirements, per-agent delivery, and the security gates around all of it. Declarative, reproducible, verifiable.
README.md-4-
README.md:5:Curator is implemented in Go and follows the [Curator Specification](https://github.com/relux-works/curator-spec), an open protocol for skill packages, project manifests, installation semantics, and the audit registry; sections are cited across this repository as `Spec §N.M`.
